1
00:00:01,350 --> 00:00:03,390
Hey! What's wrong, Tsubasa?

2
00:00:03,730 --> 00:00:05,520
Can't you solve it?

3
00:00:07,320 --> 00:00:12,040
If you continue at this level, even if you win the tournament, you won't be able to go to Brazil.

4
00:00:12,040 --> 00:00:14,400
Yes, that might be a problem...

5
00:00:16,180 --> 00:00:18,280
Carlos, let's take a short break, okay?

6
00:00:18,280 --> 00:00:21,940
No! You can't take a break in football!

7
00:00:21,940 --> 00:00:23,290
From Wakabayashi!

8
00:00:24,080 --> 00:00:27,270
What's up, Tsubasa?

9
00:00:27,270 --> 00:00:33,300
Since joining the club in Hamburg, I've been training every day.

10
00:00:33,300 --> 00:00:37,800
The traditional tournament in Japan is about to start, isn't it?

11
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:41,810
I'm tired of hearing them praise your victories.

12
00:00:41,810 --> 00:00:45,080
From now on, only let me know if you lose.

13
00:00:45,080 --> 00:00:47,810
I'm very interested in someone who can beat you.

14
00:00:48,480 --> 00:00:51,320
Actually, the reason I'm sending you this email is

15
00:00:51,320 --> 00:00:56,920
because I've met someone around your age who is very talented.

16
00:00:58,870 --> 00:01:00,360
Wakabayashi!

17
00:01:12,490 --> 00:01:14,050
Mi...

18
00:01:14,050 --> 00:01:16,430
Misaki!

19
00:01:16,430 --> 00:01:17,360
Guess who.

20
00:01:17,360 --> 00:01:19,970
Taro Misaki!

21
00:01:19,970 --> 00:01:35,020
'Anime Severler' Wishes You a Good Watch!
Instagram: AnimeSeverlerrr
Translator; Brook (Soul King)

22
00:01:22,230 --> 00:01:24,940
Ai! Ai! Ai!

23
00:01:22,230 --> 00:01:24,940
Love! Love! Love!

24
00:01:25,850 --> 00:01:28,520
Ai! Ai! Ai!

25
00:01:25,850 --> 00:01:28,520
Love! Love! Love!

26
00:01:29,440 --> 00:01:32,150
Ai! Ai! Ai!

27
00:01:29,440 --> 00:01:32,150
Love! Love! Love!

28
00:01:39,030 --> 00:01:41,870
moeru you ni hitori demo

29
00:01:39,030 --> 00:01:41,870
I keep lying to myself.

30
00:01:41,870 --> 00:01:48,130
ikiteyukeru to usobuite hashiritsudzukete

31
00:01:41,870 --> 00:01:48,130
I tell myself I can live alone, even if loneliness burns me.

32
00:01:48,130 --> 00:01:54,010
unubore no morosa wo kimi wa shitteta na no ni

33
00:01:48,130 --> 00:01:54,010
You knew how fragile my arrogance is.

34
00:01:54,010 --> 00:02:00,600
kokoro made uchinomaresareta kono yoru ni

35
00:01:54,010 --> 00:02:00,600
On this night when even my heart is shattered,

36
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:04,600
kimi no koe sagasu

37
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:04,600
I hate being helpless.

38
00:02:04,600 --> 00:02:09,110
kono yowasa ga nikui yo

39
00:02:04,600 --> 00:02:09,110
Longing for your voice.

40
00:02:09,110 --> 00:02:14,650
ima sugu torimodoshi ni ikanakya

41
00:02:09,110 --> 00:02:14,650
"I have to get you back right now!"

42
00:02:14,650 --> 00:02:16,240
baka darou?

43
00:02:14,650 --> 00:02:16,240
I'm a fool, aren't I?

44
00:02:16,240 --> 00:02:17,450
ai

45
00:02:16,240 --> 00:02:17,450
Love!

46
00:02:17,450 --> 00:02:20,950
kizudarake no ai wo shinjite

47
00:02:17,450 --> 00:02:20,950
Believing in my wounded love...

48
00:02:20,950 --> 00:02:30,840
nagareochita namida sae mo tsuyosa e to kaete

49
00:02:20,950 --> 00:02:30,840
I will turn these buried tears into strength.

50
00:02:30,840 --> 00:02:31,670
ai

51
00:02:30,840 --> 00:02:31,670
Love!

52
00:02:31,670 --> 00:02:35,470
kizudarake no ai da to shite mo

53
00:02:31,670 --> 00:02:35,470
Even though it's a wounded love,

54
00:02:35,470 --> 00:02:39,470
bokura no sekai wo tomoshiteru

55
00:02:35,470 --> 00:02:39,470
it illuminates my world.

56
00:02:39,470 --> 00:02:45,730
kono ai mo ichido taritomo

57
00:02:39,470 --> 00:02:45,730
Not even for a moment

58
00:02:45,730 --> 00:02:48,520
hanasanai

59
00:02:45,730 --> 00:02:48,520
will I let this love go!

60
00:02:50,270 --> 00:02:54,770
EPISODE 34:
THE CURTAIN RISES ON THE FIERCE BATTLE!
THE TOURNAMENT BEGINS!

61
00:02:50,600 --> 00:02:52,580
Pass it here.

62
00:02:52,580 --> 00:02:53,270
Run!

63
00:02:54,340 --> 00:02:57,370
So you're living in France now.

64
00:02:57,370 --> 00:02:59,280
France is the country of painters.

65
00:02:59,280 --> 00:03:02,380
As I recall, your father was a painter.

66
00:03:02,380 --> 00:03:03,950
You remember correctly.

67
00:03:04,800 --> 00:03:09,080
The times I spent with you all at Nankatsu never leave my mind.

68
00:03:09,670 --> 00:03:13,940
That ball sits in the place of honor in my home.

69
00:03:13,940 --> 00:03:16,490
Mine too.

70
00:03:16,490 --> 00:03:17,700
Time flows like water.

71
00:03:17,700 --> 00:03:21,270
Three years have passed since we parted ways with Tsubasa.

72
00:03:21,270 --> 00:03:23,240
But you coming to see me

73
00:03:23,240 --> 00:03:25,560
surprised me.

74
00:03:25,560 --> 00:03:31,670
I'm on summer vacation. I also learned some German.

75
00:03:31,670 --> 00:03:32,810
Is that so?

76
00:03:32,810 --> 00:03:37,990
Since you cut off contact with us, I and the others at Nankatsu worried about you.

77
00:03:37,990 --> 00:03:39,040
Sorry.

78
00:03:39,040 --> 00:03:41,740
I was busy adapting to a new life in France.

79
00:03:41,740 --> 00:03:47,490
Recently, I saw an article about you in a French football magazine.

80
00:03:47,490 --> 00:03:50,130
Did that prompt you to visit?

81
00:03:50,130 --> 00:03:53,250
Yes. It seems you're doing quite well here.

82
00:03:53,250 --> 00:03:55,320
No, I'm not good enough yet.

83
00:03:55,320 --> 00:03:58,790
You say I'm doing well, but I'm in the second division.

84
00:03:58,790 --> 00:04:04,180
But I'll set foot on a professional league pitch before I turn 18.

85
00:04:04,180 --> 00:04:06,260
I'm sure you will.

86
00:04:06,260 --> 00:04:12,240
By the way, Misaki, you're still playing football, right?

87
00:04:12,240 --> 00:04:13,600
Of course!

88
00:04:14,900 --> 00:04:18,690
Wherever I am in Japan, I can play football...

89
00:04:18,690 --> 00:04:23,800
Football is more popular in Europe compared to Japan. Especially in France.

90
00:04:23,800 --> 00:04:26,140
Wherever I go, I can play football.

91
00:04:26,140 --> 00:04:27,150
Is that so?

92
00:04:27,150 --> 00:04:29,410
That's a relief to hear.

93
00:04:29,410 --> 00:04:36,420
French football is closer to the Latin style. A person can show their individual talents there. That's rare in Europe.

94
00:04:36,420 --> 00:04:40,420
That suits your style quite well.

95
00:04:40,420 --> 00:04:43,380
We finally got to meet, Misaki.

96
00:04:43,380 --> 00:04:45,150
How about joining the game?

97
00:04:45,150 --> 00:04:48,180
Of course, let's join, Wakabayashi!

98
00:04:48,180 --> 00:04:49,020
Hey!

99
00:04:49,020 --> 00:04:50,680
Make way, your seniors are coming!

100
00:04:56,260 --> 00:04:57,860
We can't get the ball...

101
00:04:58,580 --> 00:05:00,190
Misaki...

102
00:05:00,690 --> 00:05:05,320
Tsubasa, Misaki still controls the ball very well.

103
00:05:06,200 --> 00:05:07,660
I saw it with my own eyes.

104
00:05:07,660 --> 00:05:09,120
Alright, here I go!

105
00:05:10,760 --> 00:05:15,480
Taro Misaki... He will definitely become a professional player soon.

106
00:05:15,480 --> 00:05:16,460
Oh...

107
00:05:17,250 --> 00:05:18,490
You're incredible!

108
00:05:18,490 --> 00:05:20,500
How can we become as good as you?

109
00:05:20,500 --> 00:05:25,640
Well... you could start by practicing.

110
00:05:25,640 --> 00:05:29,970
Practice 365 days a year. Never let the ball leave your side.

111
00:05:29,970 --> 00:05:31,970
"The ball is your friend."

112
00:05:31,970 --> 00:05:36,980
A valuable teammate said that when I played in Japan.

113
00:05:40,670 --> 00:05:42,880
Here's a photo from that day.

114
00:05:42,880 --> 00:05:45,530
I also got your address in France.

115
00:05:45,530 --> 00:05:50,280
Tsubasa, work hard to win the traditional tournament for the third time.

116
00:05:50,820 --> 00:05:52,440
That's all for today.

117
00:05:52,440 --> 00:05:53,500
Greetings from Germany,

118
00:05:53,500 --> 00:05:55,330
Genzo Wakabayashi.

119
00:05:55,330 --> 00:05:58,610
So Misaki has been in France all this time.

120
00:05:58,610 --> 00:06:01,340
That's why he didn't participate in any tournaments in Japan.

121
00:06:02,630 --> 00:06:04,810
But... I'm quite happy.

122
00:06:04,810 --> 00:06:09,010
Misaki is doing well and still playing football.

123
00:06:09,950 --> 00:06:11,930
Wakabayashi is in Germany,

124
00:06:11,930 --> 00:06:13,950
and Misaki is in France.

125
00:06:13,950 --> 00:06:18,170
Now it's my turn to go to Brazil and become a professional player!

126
00:06:18,170 --> 00:06:22,480
Then together we can make Japanese football the best in the world.

127
00:06:22,480 --> 00:06:26,150
That's my dream.

128
00:06:26,150 --> 00:06:28,580
Alright Carlos, break's over!

129
00:06:28,580 --> 00:06:29,640
Let's get to work!

130
00:06:29,640 --> 00:06:31,910
The match is still on, isn't it?

131
00:06:31,910 --> 00:06:33,920
So what's the answer to the last question?

132
00:06:33,920 --> 00:06:35,710
That's a piece of cake for me.

133
00:06:37,580 --> 00:06:39,920
What? You're going back by bullet train?

134
00:06:39,920 --> 00:06:41,410
Exactly!

135
00:06:41,410 --> 00:06:47,720
I was planning to stay at your place and observe Nankatsu's practices,

136
00:06:47,720 --> 00:06:48,920
but I changed my mind.

137
00:06:48,920 --> 00:06:52,250
While watching the final matches of Nankatsu and Toho,

138
00:06:52,250 --> 00:06:54,930
I realized we shouldn't be so confident.

139
00:06:54,930 --> 00:06:57,240
We're going back to Nagasaki.

140
00:06:57,240 --> 00:07:00,080
And we'll train intensely until the tournament starts.

141
00:07:00,080 --> 00:07:03,100
I took some very important notes.

142
00:07:03,100 --> 00:07:05,940
Yukari, send my message to the guys at Nankatsu:

143
00:07:05,940 --> 00:07:12,700
This year, in the traditional tournament, Hirado Middle School won't let them win their 3rd championship.

144
00:07:17,200 --> 00:07:19,090
Coach, can I come in? It's Sawada.

145
00:07:19,090 --> 00:07:20,580
Come in.

146
00:07:20,580 --> 00:07:22,210
Coach, there's a problem with the captain.

147
00:07:22,210 --> 00:07:24,710
I looked everywhere. I can't find Hyuga.

148
00:07:24,710 --> 00:07:26,500
What did you say?

149
00:07:32,060 --> 00:07:34,400
So I've lost my will to fight, huh?

150
00:07:34,400 --> 00:07:36,430
A caged tiger, am I?

151
00:07:40,690 --> 00:07:41,580
Whaaat?

152
00:07:41,580 --> 00:07:43,190
Misaki is in France?

153
00:07:43,190 --> 00:07:44,260
There.

154
00:07:44,260 --> 00:07:45,190
Let me see...

155
00:07:46,030 --> 00:07:49,300
Wow, Misaki is in France!

156
00:07:50,320 --> 00:07:52,790
He's so cute....

157
00:07:52,790 --> 00:07:53,950
Who is this?

158
00:07:53,950 --> 00:07:57,690
That's Misaki, a former player of Nankatsu SC.

159
00:07:57,690 --> 00:08:00,620
He and Tsubasa were known as the legendary duo.

160
00:08:00,620 --> 00:08:03,120
That's amazing!

161
00:08:03,120 --> 00:08:04,610
I didn't expect that.

162
00:08:04,610 --> 00:08:07,180
He looks very innocent.

163
00:08:07,180 --> 00:08:10,960
But... Tsubasa is still the best!

164
00:08:10,960 --> 00:08:12,910
What's with the "but," Kumi?

165
00:08:12,910 --> 00:08:15,140
N-Nothing!

166
00:08:15,140 --> 00:08:21,840
Nankatsu Middle School, captained by Tsubasa, aims for their first-ever 3rd championship.

167
00:08:21,840 --> 00:08:27,530
At the same time, rival teams are trying to prevent his streak from reaching three at all costs.

168
00:08:26,690 --> 00:08:30,360
HOKKAIDO - FURANO MIDDLE SCHOOL

169
00:08:27,530 --> 00:08:30,270
We will dethrone Nankatsu!

170
00:08:30,270 --> 00:08:31,440
Yes!

171
00:08:32,150 --> 00:08:33,100
We did it!

172
00:08:32,450 --> 00:08:36,490
AKITA - HANAWA MIDDLE SCHOOL

173
00:08:33,100 --> 00:08:34,430
We finally did it!

174
00:08:34,430 --> 00:08:36,550
This is our new combination!

175
00:08:36,550 --> 00:08:39,030
Yes, we finally did it, Masao!

176
00:08:39,080 --> 00:08:43,080
OSAKA - AZUMAICHI MIDDLE SCHOOL

177
00:08:39,710 --> 00:08:41,760
And new challengers are emerging!

178
00:08:41,760 --> 00:08:44,460
Our first participation will be our first championship!

179
00:08:44,460 --> 00:08:46,210
What's wrong with you?

180
00:08:46,210 --> 00:08:49,210
Don't think you can beat Nankatsu or Toho in this state.

181
00:08:46,290 --> 00:08:50,550
NAGASAKI - HIRADO MIDDLE SCHOOL

182
00:08:49,210 --> 00:08:50,490
Yes!

183
00:08:50,490 --> 00:08:56,720
As the Traditional Tournament draws near, all teams continue their training with great ambition.

184
00:08:57,460 --> 00:08:59,720
Likewise in Okinawa...

185
00:08:59,720 --> 00:09:01,020
What's wrong with you?

186
00:09:01,020 --> 00:09:05,730
It's because you give up so easily that everyone says Japanese football's fallen behind!

187
00:09:05,730 --> 00:09:08,630
Use this sandy beach to increase the strength in your legs.

188
00:09:08,630 --> 00:09:10,820
In football, everything comes from the legs.

189
00:09:10,820 --> 00:09:11,730
Yes!

190
00:09:12,230 --> 00:09:13,610
Coach Kira...

191
00:09:13,610 --> 00:09:17,770
So you came, Kojiro.

192
00:09:17,770 --> 00:09:18,540
Yes.

193
00:09:20,960 --> 00:09:22,370
What does this mean?

194
00:09:22,370 --> 00:09:24,040
There's only one week left.

195
00:09:24,040 --> 00:09:27,330
What is going through your mind?

196
00:09:27,330 --> 00:09:28,500
Coach!

197
00:09:28,500 --> 00:09:32,440
Captain Gaiba went to Okinawa, to Coach Kira.

198
00:09:32,440 --> 00:09:33,260
What did you say?

199
00:09:33,260 --> 00:09:34,680
Coach Kira?

200
00:09:34,680 --> 00:09:36,280
Who is that?

201
00:09:36,280 --> 00:09:38,010
And did you say Okinawa?

202
00:09:38,010 --> 00:09:39,810
Yes.

203
00:09:39,810 --> 00:09:43,020
Hyuga came here as a scholarship student.

204
00:09:43,020 --> 00:09:44,780
Moreover, he is the captain of this team.

205
00:09:44,780 --> 00:09:49,520
How can he act so selfishly when the traditional tournament is about to begin?

206
00:09:49,520 --> 00:09:51,480
I will never tolerate such behavior.

207
00:09:51,480 --> 00:09:55,190
But I'm sure he'll come back before the tournament.

208
00:09:55,190 --> 00:09:58,320
Enough! If he doesn't come, that's fine with me!

209
00:09:58,320 --> 00:10:03,080
In response, I'm canceling his high school and university scholarship.

210
00:10:03,080 --> 00:10:04,080
What?!

211
00:10:04,080 --> 00:10:06,580
We'll go to the traditional tournament without him.

212
00:10:06,580 --> 00:10:07,940
Co—

213
00:10:07,940 --> 00:10:09,580
Coach!

214
00:10:10,130 --> 00:10:13,040
THE DAY BEFORE THE TOURNAMENT

215
00:10:13,040 --> 00:10:16,130
Ohhh, we could finally relax a bit.

216
00:10:16,920 --> 00:10:20,970
Hey! As expected, we're seen as the strongest team in the tournament.

217
00:10:20,970 --> 00:10:22,470
Let me see that.

218
00:10:23,240 --> 00:10:26,160
Katagiri from the Federation also has an article here.

219
00:10:26,160 --> 00:10:27,000
Eh—

220
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:33,480
It says: In this age group, there is no one who can beat the future ace of Japanese football, Tsubasa.

221
00:10:33,480 --> 00:10:37,700
Even for a Tsubasa fanatic, that's definitely an exaggeration.

222
00:10:37,700 --> 00:10:41,160
Hyuga and the others will go crazy when they see this.

223
00:10:43,020 --> 00:10:44,950
You have no rivals.

224
00:10:44,950 --> 00:10:47,830
I wrote my honest thoughts.

225
00:10:48,760 --> 00:10:52,910
But this might put pressure on Tsubasa.

226
00:10:52,910 --> 00:10:59,340
So, a player who can beat you might emerge.

227
00:11:00,580 --> 00:11:03,640
Mr. Katagiri, even if you think so, I will never lose.

228
00:11:03,640 --> 00:11:09,240
If I'm not the best in Japan, even going to Brazil will be meaningless.

229
00:11:09,240 --> 00:11:10,760
What is this?

230
00:11:11,350 --> 00:11:13,910
What are you fixated on, Ishizaki?

231
00:11:13,910 --> 00:11:15,110
Just look at this.

232
00:11:15,110 --> 00:11:18,110
NEWS - INFO
Toho's captain Hyuga has disappeared! Coach Kitazume says "We'll continue without him."

233
00:11:18,110 --> 00:11:20,020
T-This...

234
00:11:20,020 --> 00:11:21,740
Hyuga has disappeared.

235
00:11:21,740 --> 00:11:22,980
W-What?!

236
00:11:24,040 --> 00:11:29,040
~Anime Severler~
Instagram: AnimeSeverlerrr

237
00:11:33,820 --> 00:11:38,130
The large typhoon number 7 is about to reach Okinawa.

238
00:11:38,130 --> 00:11:42,860
There will be high waves along the coast; you are advised to be careful.

239
00:11:56,070 --> 00:11:57,480
Come on!

240
00:12:06,820 --> 00:12:09,200
Damn it!

241
00:12:09,200 --> 00:12:14,960
Look at that kid from Tokyo, he's still training.

242
00:12:14,960 --> 00:12:16,920
Shouldn't we stop him?

243
00:12:16,920 --> 00:12:18,920
He doesn't look like he did yesterday.

244
00:12:18,920 --> 00:12:22,790
It seems Coach Kira had him working until past midnight yesterday.

245
00:12:22,790 --> 00:12:24,430
Get up, Kojiro!

246
00:12:24,430 --> 00:12:27,180
That's enough to make this guy tremble.

247
00:12:28,100 --> 00:12:31,980
Is it really necessary to work this hard for football...?

248
00:12:37,160 --> 00:12:38,190
Kojiro.

249
00:12:43,510 --> 00:12:44,530
I...

250
00:12:45,440 --> 00:12:46,760
I...

251
00:12:49,030 --> 00:12:50,970
...I'm tired of losing every time...!

252
00:12:52,040 --> 00:12:58,960
I'm tired of losing to Tsubasa Ozora!

253
00:13:02,470 --> 00:13:06,970
The power of your explosive shot was enough to pierce through these waves...

254
00:13:06,970 --> 00:13:13,480
And on top of that, while the waves are pushing your legs this hard...

255
00:13:13,480 --> 00:13:16,230
Did you finally do it, Kojiro?

256
00:13:21,230 --> 00:13:24,140
This fighting spirit of yours...

257
00:13:24,140 --> 00:13:26,240
The tiger has awakened from its sleep

258
00:13:27,490 --> 00:13:32,400
and has unsheathed its claws again.

259
00:13:35,500 --> 00:13:39,000
TOURNAMENT DAY

260
00:13:36,180 --> 00:13:39,000
And finally, Tournament Day has arrived.

261
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:40,620
Hurry up, get inside, kids!

262
00:13:40,620 --> 00:13:42,010
We're going.

263
00:13:42,010 --> 00:13:43,510
Y-Yes, Coach!

264
00:13:43,510 --> 00:13:45,020
No way...

265
00:13:45,020 --> 00:13:47,540
Hyuga still hasn't come.

266
00:13:47,540 --> 00:13:50,260
Will we go into the battle without our captain?

267
00:13:57,410 --> 00:13:58,270
Kojiro.

268
00:13:59,640 --> 00:14:00,810
Kojiro!

269
00:14:04,750 --> 00:14:06,900
Get up, Kojiro!

270
00:14:08,340 --> 00:14:10,410
Coach Kira.

271
00:14:11,040 --> 00:14:13,910
You endured this tough week well.

272
00:14:16,910 --> 00:14:19,670
Here's your plane ticket to Tokyo.

273
00:14:19,670 --> 00:14:23,420
Go now, Kojiro! Go and unleash your storm!

274
00:14:24,620 --> 00:14:26,170
Definitely!

275
00:14:27,360 --> 00:14:28,340
Hurry up.

276
00:14:28,340 --> 00:14:30,550
If we don't hurry, Nankatsu will leave the hotel.

277
00:14:30,550 --> 00:14:34,040
Before that, we must get an interview with Tsubasa no matter what.

278
00:14:34,040 --> 00:14:35,060
Yes, sir.

279
00:14:36,060 --> 00:14:37,000
Whoa!

280
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:38,670
Sir, this...

281
00:14:39,970 --> 00:14:41,180
Tsubasa!

282
00:14:41,180 --> 00:14:42,360
What is he doing there?

283
00:14:49,660 --> 00:14:51,030
What?!

284
00:14:51,030 --> 00:14:52,410
Could that shot be...

285
00:14:53,990 --> 00:14:55,790
Still not good enough!

286
00:14:56,650 --> 00:15:00,730
"Tsubasa, add spin to your long shots."

287
00:15:00,730 --> 00:15:04,250
If you don't master this shot, you can't become a first-class player.

288
00:15:04,250 --> 00:15:08,510
The ball dips downward after passing the goalkeeper in the air.

289
00:15:08,510 --> 00:15:15,260
Tsubasa, this is Brazil level... No, this is a world-class shot.

290
00:15:15,970 --> 00:15:19,940
Roberto, I will definitely win the tournament.

291
00:15:20,580 --> 00:15:21,950
And then...

292
00:15:26,940 --> 00:15:29,200
The opening ceremony is about to begin.

293
00:15:29,200 --> 00:15:31,950
It seems there was a typhoon in Okinawa yesterday.

294
00:15:31,950 --> 00:15:34,300
But here, in Saitama, the weather is completely clear!

295
00:15:34,300 --> 00:15:37,450
The scorching August sun makes the field brilliantly bright.

296
00:15:38,240 --> 00:15:42,290
The first to enter the field, the center of all attention, aiming for the first-ever triple championship streak in history,

297
00:15:42,290 --> 00:15:47,960
and representing the Shizuoka region, Nankatsu MS.

298
00:15:47,960 --> 00:15:51,090
FURANO MIDDLE SCHOOL
HOKKAIDO

299
00:15:47,960 --> 00:15:51,840
The representatives from the other 46 regions are also preparing

300
00:15:51,840 --> 00:15:53,840
and entering the field in rows.

301
00:15:54,720 --> 00:15:57,170
The tournament will be in an elimination format.

302
00:15:57,170 --> 00:15:59,850
One loss is enough to be eliminated.

303
00:15:59,850 --> 00:16:06,770
All of them are aiming for the bright red championship flag.

304
00:16:06,770 --> 00:16:08,890
We'll take it this year.

305
00:16:08,890 --> 00:16:10,280
Of course we'll take it!

306
00:16:10,280 --> 00:16:11,780
Hmph.

307
00:16:11,780 --> 00:16:14,530
No need to argue, the flag is ours this year.

308
00:16:14,530 --> 00:16:17,930
We'll return to Hokkaido with the flag this year!

309
00:16:17,930 --> 00:16:19,030
Isn't that right, guys?

310
00:16:19,030 --> 00:16:20,040
That's right!

311
00:16:20,540 --> 00:16:22,270
I won't give it to anyone.

312
00:16:22,270 --> 00:16:25,140
On the final day of the tournament,

313
00:16:25,140 --> 00:16:27,040
I will raise the championship flag.

314
00:16:27,040 --> 00:16:29,100
Hey, look at that.

315
00:16:30,420 --> 00:16:33,720
Do you see? Hyuga isn't among the Toho team.

316
00:16:33,720 --> 00:16:35,510
Yeah, you're right.

317
00:16:36,520 --> 00:16:37,800
Sanae.

318
00:16:39,620 --> 00:16:40,720
It's been a while.

319
00:16:40,720 --> 00:16:42,190
Yayoi!

320
00:16:42,190 --> 00:16:43,230
Jun, come here!

321
00:16:43,860 --> 00:16:45,350
Jun?

322
00:16:45,350 --> 00:16:47,400
Hey, long time no see.

323
00:16:47,400 --> 00:16:48,980
Misugi!

324
00:16:48,980 --> 00:16:49,860
Ba-dump!

325
00:16:51,360 --> 00:16:54,010
Yukari, get a grip!

326
00:16:55,770 --> 00:16:57,740
So now it's Jun instead of Captain, huh.

327
00:16:57,740 --> 00:17:00,600
You're embarrassing me, Sanae...!

328
00:17:00,600 --> 00:17:04,760
By the way, you came really close in the Tokyo tournament, didn't you, Misugi?

329
00:17:07,380 --> 00:17:10,130
I did the best I could.

330
00:17:10,130 --> 00:17:12,490
The opening ceremony is over.

331
00:17:12,490 --> 00:17:14,490
The first match will start immediately.

332
00:17:14,490 --> 00:17:17,840
The match will be between last year's champion, Nankatsu MS,

333
00:17:17,840 --> 00:17:20,190
and Azumaichi MS from Osaka, participating in the tournament for the first time.

334
00:17:20,190 --> 00:17:25,760
Then we'll conclude the day by watching a match between Toho Academy and Matsukami MS.

335
00:17:25,760 --> 00:17:29,730
So most of the participating teams will just watch the matches today.

336
00:17:29,730 --> 00:17:32,480
Well, let's see how you play.

337
00:17:32,480 --> 00:17:35,740
I wonder what kind of game Nankatsu will play.

338
00:17:36,400 --> 00:17:37,340
Mr. Mikami.

339
00:17:37,340 --> 00:17:38,160
Hmm?

340
00:17:38,160 --> 00:17:40,490
Hello, Katagiri.

341
00:17:40,490 --> 00:17:42,450
Did you come to observe Nankatsu?

342
00:17:42,450 --> 00:17:44,480
Yes, you could say that.

343
00:17:44,480 --> 00:17:49,460
But... they say this generation is at a higher level than the previous one.

344
00:17:49,460 --> 00:17:54,480
You never know where and when a great player will emerge.

345
00:17:54,480 --> 00:17:59,320
Your prediction might come true from the first game.

346
00:18:00,750 --> 00:18:04,110
This time, luck isn't really on our side.

347
00:18:04,110 --> 00:18:07,310
Hanawa and the Tachibana twins are right next to us.

348
00:18:07,310 --> 00:18:10,660
Furano is also in the next bracket.

349
00:18:10,660 --> 00:18:15,240
If things go as usual, your opponents will be tough until the final against Toho.

350
00:18:15,240 --> 00:18:17,740
It doesn't matter who we play against.

351
00:18:17,740 --> 00:18:20,740
This is our last year in this tournament.

352
00:18:20,740 --> 00:18:22,950
Of course we won't let anyone beat us!

353
00:18:24,900 --> 00:18:25,870
Manabu.

354
00:18:26,460 --> 00:18:29,420
What kind of information do you have on our first opponent, Azumaichi?

355
00:18:29,420 --> 00:18:31,680
They're participating in the tournament for the first time.

356
00:18:31,680 --> 00:18:35,550
That's the team that beat Naniwa, the one with Nakanishi, right?

357
00:18:35,550 --> 00:18:37,050
Yes.

358
00:18:37,050 --> 00:18:39,100
A quick attack after a tight defense;

359
00:18:39,100 --> 00:18:43,280
It seems they used counter-attacks to beat the Osaka region.

360
00:18:43,280 --> 00:18:48,620
Azumaichi has its own unique playing style.

361
00:18:49,190 --> 00:18:51,460
He is their goal scorer.

362
00:18:51,460 --> 00:18:54,420
But he's not a forward; he's their defender.

363
00:18:54,420 --> 00:18:55,440
Huh?!

364
00:18:55,440 --> 00:18:59,400
#7, Makoto Soda, the center of the defense.

365
00:18:59,400 --> 00:19:05,280
He's the center of their defense, but at the same time, a goal scorer who rarely misses a shot.

366
00:19:06,040 --> 00:19:07,990
A counter-defender, huh?

367
00:19:07,990 --> 00:19:09,030
That's interesting.

368
00:19:09,030 --> 00:19:10,740
It makes me even more excited.

369
00:19:10,740 --> 00:19:16,450
If that's the case, as our defense, how about scoring the first goal of the tournament?

370
00:19:16,450 --> 00:19:18,920
Yeah, I'm in!

371
00:19:18,920 --> 00:19:21,330
I was joking.

372
00:19:22,930 --> 00:19:24,860
Guys, the match is about to start.

373
00:19:24,860 --> 00:19:27,020
Go outside and warm up!

374
00:19:27,020 --> 00:19:28,270
Yes, Coach!

375
00:19:28,270 --> 00:19:30,270
AZUMAICHI MIDDLE SCHOOL
OSAKA

376
00:19:29,520 --> 00:19:30,270
Listen to me!

377
00:19:30,270 --> 00:19:33,780
In the end, what we call Nankatsu is entirely about Tsubasa Ozora!

378
00:19:33,780 --> 00:19:36,930
If we can neutralize him, we can win!

379
00:19:36,930 --> 00:19:37,960
Okay, Coach!

380
00:19:37,960 --> 00:19:42,090
Soda, I want you to mark him. I expect you to do it successfully.

381
00:19:42,090 --> 00:19:43,660
Leave that to me.

382
00:19:43,660 --> 00:19:47,680
Just the thought of beating Tsubasa Ozora

383
00:19:47,680 --> 00:19:49,940
in front of such a large crowd makes me happy.

384
00:19:49,940 --> 00:19:53,920
I'll show them who I am.

385
00:19:54,940 --> 00:19:58,960
On the other side, Toho Academy has arrived at Bay Coas Stadium.

386
00:19:58,960 --> 00:20:01,970
The other match is currently on hold.

387
00:20:02,660 --> 00:20:05,260
Our match will start in 90 minutes.

388
00:20:05,260 --> 00:20:08,050
Rest well until then.

389
00:20:08,050 --> 00:20:09,470
Okay, Coach!

390
00:20:09,880 --> 00:20:10,480
Huh?

391
00:20:10,480 --> 00:20:11,270
Oh!

392
00:20:13,350 --> 00:20:15,540
Captain!

393
00:20:15,540 --> 00:20:16,480
Hyuga!

394
00:20:17,760 --> 00:20:21,990
Coach, I've returned from Okinawa.

395
00:20:26,460 --> 00:20:29,880
Hyuga, I can't let you play in this tournament.

396
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:33,340
C-Coach!

397
00:20:33,340 --> 00:20:34,250
Hyuga!

398
00:20:42,760 --> 00:20:44,460
Hurry up!

399
00:20:47,160 --> 00:20:49,140
Looks like we arrived just in time!

400
00:20:49,140 --> 00:20:52,640
Come on, crush them!

401
00:20:52,930 --> 00:20:56,190
GO! GO! Nankatsu!

402
00:20:56,190 --> 00:20:57,990
Ishizaki!

403
00:20:58,690 --> 00:21:00,980
As promised, we came to support you!

404
00:21:00,980 --> 00:21:02,580
Ah, Urabe and the others have come!

405
00:21:02,580 --> 00:21:05,930
You are Shizuoka's representatives!

406
00:21:05,930 --> 00:21:07,570
Don't come back without the championship!

407
00:21:07,570 --> 00:21:09,570
Otherwise, I won't go easy on you!

408
00:21:09,570 --> 00:21:11,100
Definitely trust us!

409
00:21:11,100 --> 00:21:14,040
Hey, get a grip!

410
00:21:14,040 --> 00:21:14,580
What did you say?!

411
00:21:14,970 --> 00:21:18,170
Don't be overconfident just because you won twice.

412
00:21:18,170 --> 00:21:19,870
Say that again, punk!

413
00:21:19,870 --> 00:21:20,750
Ishizaki.

414
00:21:22,700 --> 00:21:24,850
That goes for you too, Tsubasa Ozora.

415
00:21:24,850 --> 00:21:27,680
You don't look all that intimidating.

416
00:21:27,680 --> 00:21:30,060
I'll be marking you, so let's be nice to each other.

417
00:21:30,060 --> 00:21:33,060
Hey, watch your mouth.

418
00:21:33,060 --> 00:21:36,810
Even if it's before the match, if you keep this up, I'll have you removed.

419
00:21:36,810 --> 00:21:38,200
Go to your spot!

420
00:21:38,200 --> 00:21:40,320
Alright, okay, okay, got it.

421
00:21:41,740 --> 00:21:44,820
This is Makoto Soda.

422
00:21:44,820 --> 00:21:48,540
Nankatsu won the coin toss and took the ball.

423
00:21:48,540 --> 00:21:52,160
Both teams have taken their positions.

424
00:21:52,160 --> 00:21:54,290
Let's start the first match.

425
00:21:54,290 --> 00:21:56,540
We'll be champions again!

426
00:21:56,540 --> 00:21:58,290
The 3rd one is coming!

427
00:21:58,290 --> 00:21:59,540
I'll protect it!

428
00:21:59,540 --> 00:22:01,130
I'll attack!

429
00:22:01,130 --> 00:22:06,880
The eagerly awaited match begins!

430
00:22:08,800 --> 00:22:10,000
Fools.

431
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:13,130
You won't get the 3rd championship!

432
00:22:17,130 --> 00:22:32,130
